      <IncidentDescription>During the passing period before fifth-period Earth Science, Teodoro Delgado disclosed to Assistant Principal Chiamaka Okafor that he had a small pocketknife and a canister of pepper spray in his backpack. The items were secured in the North Courtyard without being displayed, used, or directed toward any person. Solenne Boudreaux was identified as a nearby student witness and reported no injury. The incident was documented, guardians were contacted, and a restorative reentry meeting was arranged.</IncidentDescription>
